Solutions Attempted: Making Local n8n Public for Webhook
Problem Recap
n8n was running locally on http://localhost:5678. Meta (and Evolution API) can only call a public HTTPS URL. Localhost cannot be reached from outside → webhook verification failed.
We tried two free tunneling tools to expose your local n8n.
1. ngrok (Quick Tunnel) – First Attempt
Step-by-step commands we used:
Download and install ngrok from https://ngrok.com/download (Windows/Mac/Linux).
Open terminal / command prompt and run these commands one by one:
Bash
# 1. Add your free ngrok auth token (get it from https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken)
ngrok config add-authtoken YOUR_NGROK_AUTHTOKEN_HERE

# 2. Start the tunnel on n8n's default port
ngrok http 5678
ngrok will show a public URL like this:
text
https://abc123.ngrok.io
Copy the https URL and paste it into Meta’s Callback URL field, like this:
text
https://abc123.ngrok.io/webhook-test/0b1b3a9b-2f6a-4f5a-8385-6365d96f4802
Keep Verify Token as test123 → Click Verify and save.
Note: The ngrok URL changes every time you restart it (free plan). For testing it works great.

2. Cloudflare Tunnel – Second Attempt
Step-by-step commands we used:
Go to https://one.dash.cloudflare.com/ → Log in with your Cloudflare account (or create one).
In the dashboard:
Left menu → Networks → Connectors → Cloudflare Tunnels
Click Create a tunnel
Choose Cloudflared → Next
Give it a name (e.g. n8n-chatbot) → Save tunnel
Copy the installation command shown on the screen (it looks like this):
Bash
cloudflared tunnel run --token YOUR_LONG_CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN_HERE
Download and install cloudflared (the connector):
Windows/Mac/Linux: Download from https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-apps/install-and-setup/tunnel-guide/local/
In terminal / command prompt, run the command you copied:
Bash
cloudflared tunnel run --token YOUR_LONG_CLOUDFLARE_TOKEN_HERE
Go back to the Cloudflare dashboard → Add a Public Hostname:
Subdomain: anything you want (e.g. n8n-chatbot)
Domain: your Cloudflare domain (or use the free trycloudflare.com one)
Service: http://localhost:5678
Save
Your public URL will now be something like:
text
https://n8n-chatbot.yourdomain.com
Paste this public URL into Meta’s Callback URL (same as ngrok step above).
Note: Cloudflare Tunnel is more stable and the URL doesn’t change, but it requires a Cloudflare account and sometimes extra DNS setup.








