That's the problem. Meta has a very short timeout — around 5 seconds. If your n8n takes longer than that to respond, Meta rejects it even if the response is correct.
The verify response is slow because the request goes through too many nodes before responding — it hits the Code node, then the Switch node, then finally the Respond node. By then Meta has already timed out.
The fix — make a dead-simple dedicated verify endpoint that responds instantly.
